WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.025
Check yourself with two questions.

2
00:00:02.025 --> 00:00:07.337
First: an Attack Surface Reduction policy
in Intune is assigned to a user group.

3
00:00:07.337 --> 00:00:08.350
What happens?

4
00:00:08.350 --> 00:00:09.575
The answer is b.

5
00:00:09.575 --> 00:00:12.961
It never applies, because
Microsoft Learn says Defender

6
00:00:12.961 --> 00:00:16.275
for Endpoint management
supports device objects only.

7
00:00:16.275 --> 00:00:18.375
Assign it to an Entra device group.

8
00:00:18.375 --> 00:00:22.624
Second: a Zero Trust Assessment
test that needs Security

9
00:00:22.624 --> 00:00:26.150
Exposure Management is
skipped in a G C C tenant.

10
00:00:26.150 --> 00:00:27.362
How is it recorded?

11
00:00:27.362 --> 00:00:29.464
The answer is b: as not applicable,

12
00:00:29.464 --> 00:00:34.288
because Learn says Exposure Management
is available in Public Cloud only.

13
00:00:34.288 --> 00:00:38.262
A feature G C C doesn't offer
goes in the decision record and

14
00:00:38.262 --> 00:00:42.651
the closure register as a disposition,
never as a failed control.

15
00:00:42.651 --> 00:00:47.520
The module page has two more questions,
each linked to the unit that answers it.
